From dda3fd76751553b250428a2a7d027aa7f628a390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:04:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(gateway): redeliver an automated wake a held
 quota wall refused, once, after the reset

A Kanban notifier (or background-process) wake committed to a chat whose pinned route sits behind a
held subscription wall was refused before the agent was built; the held reply tells a person to
"resend after the reset", but nobody resends an automated notice, so it was lost until another event
woke the chat (hub chat local-be7f1ded..., 2026-11-14: three refused notifier wakes).

- _resolution_failure_result stamps failure_resets_at from SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable.
- gateway/session_wall_replay.py: after a pre-build wall refusal (api_calls 0, route_refused /
  auth_permanent, a known reset) of an unattended route wake (kanban-wake / background-wake, principal
  automation:<route>), plan one redelivery at max(reset + 60s, now + 60s) (none past 7 days), durable in
  state_meta and armed in-process; re-armed at authority boot. It re-admits through admit_route_wake
  under the deterministic identity tail wall-replay:<tail> (an exact replay, never folded into a
  waiting Kanban wake). A redelivery refused again plans nothing. Transient admission refusals or a
  missing adapter retry (bounded); permanent refusals drop. The refused reply (and error card) says
  when the notice will be delivered again. A person's message keeps the held reply unchanged.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_wall_replay_automation_wake.py (real runner, authority, FIFO, real held
SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable; 23 tests; 21 mutants killed, 1 equivalent check removed).
